<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">State of Grão-Pará and Maranhão</h1><p class="st-meta">1751 CE – 1772 CE · capital Belém</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Pombal's reorganised Amazon colony, ruled from Belém, where Jesuit control of indigenous peoples was ended and a monopoly company brought enslaved Africans.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1751 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marquis-of-pombal">Marquis of Pombal</a> reorganised the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-maranhao">State of Maranhão</a> as the State of Grão-Pará and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maranhao">Maranhão</a>, moving its capital from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-luis">São Luís</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belem">Belém</a>. His brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-xavier-de-mendonca-furtado">Francisco Xavier de Mendonça Furtado</a> became governor, charged with mapping the borders agreed with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-madrid-1750">Treaty of Madrid</a> and asserting royal power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amazon">Amazon</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-xavier-de-mendonca-furtado">Mendonça Furtado</a> clashed with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a>, who controlled indigenous villages and labour. In 1755 a law freed indigenous people from missionary rule, and from 1757 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diretorio-dos-indios">Directorate</a> placed their villages under lay directors and promoted Portuguese over the língua geral. The Jesuits were expelled in 1759. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/general-company-of-grao-para-and-maranhao">General Company of Grão-Pará and Maranhão</a>, founded in 1755, held a trade monopoly and imported enslaved Africans for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> plantations.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1772 the state was divided into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-grao-para-and-rio-negro">State of Grão-Pará and Rio Negro</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-maranhao-and-piaui">State of Maranhão and Piauí</a>. The trading company lost its monopoly in 1778. Its policies towards indigenous peoples shaped the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amazon">Amazon</a> for decades, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belem">Belém</a> remained the region's capital.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/state-of-grao-para-and-maranhao.jpg" alt="State of Grão-Pará and Maranhão" width="320" height="214"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan This W3C-unspecified vector image was created with Inkscape . · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Portugal_(1750).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1751 CE – 1772 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Belém</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Francisco Xavier de Mendonça Furtado</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Portuguese, Nheengatu</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/brazil">Brazil</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Estado do Grão-Pará e Maranhão</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1762&amp;focus=state-of-grao-para-and-maranhao" aria-label="State of Grão-Pará and Maranhão on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="3333 2232 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where State of Grão-Pará and Maranhão lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3653 2488L3770 2528M3653 2488L3944 2917M3653 2488L4773 1044M3653 2488L3653 2488M3653 2488L3770 2528"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3770 2528h0M3944 2917h0M4773 1044h0M3653 2488h0M3770 2528h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3653 2488h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3653 2488h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Belém. <a href="/atlas?y